Dialogue: 0,0:01:42.42,0:01:44.04,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:52.10,0:01:53.33,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Ed!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:57.60,0:02:00.39,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Humans die all too quickly.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:00.39,0:02:02.76,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother! Brother!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:02.76,0:02:05.64,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It can't be! There's no way \NBrother can be dead!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:06.43,0:02:08.10,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Dead?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:08.60,0:02:12.82,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's right, dead. \NThey'll all be dead.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:12.82,0:02:16.19,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Only the homunculi will survive.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:22.34,0:02:24.14,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother can't die!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:24.14,0:02:28.33,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's not right! Brother... Brother!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:28.55,0:02:30.48,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,This is real life.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:30.48,0:02:33.04,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Perhaps he just \Nhadn't paid enough.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:33.59,0:02:36.93,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We always come \Njust a little short of the price.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:54.85,0:02:55.90,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Hey, are you all right?!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:02.61,0:03:03.95,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Colonel Archer!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:04.77,0:03:06.79,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I need to use that car.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:07.59,0:03:09.31,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Colonel, where are you going?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:09.31,0:03:11.04,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The Führer's residence.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:11.04,0:03:13.30,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Rebels have broken in.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:13.90,0:03:16.80,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That was a misunderstanding. It was just Lt. Hawkeye there.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:18.32,0:03:20.17,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Hawkeye?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:22.04,0:03:23.89,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What is she doing here?!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:30.53,0:03:31.69,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Please stop!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:31.69,0:03:33.99,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The Führer ordered us to question her \Nat the command center!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:33.99,0:03:36.36,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What are you guys plotting?!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:36.36,0:03:37.94,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Colonel! Colonel!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:37.94,0:03:41.24,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Please calm down, Colonel!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:55.16,0:03:58.76,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,At this level, all you'll do \Nis spend my lives.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:01.30,0:04:06.93,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I was a little curious what would happen \Nif my whole body were to explode.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:08.31,0:04:11.68,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Is that how badly you want to become Führer?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:13.60,0:04:16.26,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I can see right through your petty ambitions.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:16.26,0:04:19.68,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But you should have \Nspent more time on this.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:20.12,0:04:26.03,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,After attempting assassination, you won't ever be able to sit in a seat of power again.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:26.53,0:04:30.17,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I just can't forgive myself for acting like such a fool.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:30.72,0:04:34.67,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,This is the only way I can \Nmake amends to dead friends.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:34.90,0:04:37.79,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Then go apologize to them alone.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:37.79,0:04:40.38,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Give Brig. Gen. Hughes my regards.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:45.38,0:04:46.64,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Father!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:49.32,0:04:52.31,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Not to worry. I caught the rebel.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:53.41,0:04:56.81,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm sorry I didn't follow your orders, Father,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:57.10,0:05:00.23,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,but I wanted to pay you back for looking after me.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:06.28,0:05:10.60,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,This is one of the humans \Nwhom you said were foolish.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:13.84,0:05:16.83,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Father? What is the matter, Father?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:17.07,0:05:19.84,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What have you done?!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:20.84,0:05:24.08,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,U-Um... I took this out of the safe.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:24.08,0:05:27.05,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I didn't want your precious things \Nto be lost if there was a fire, Father.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:29.66,0:05:32.25,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Father...
Dialogue: 0,0:05:43.02,0:05:45.74,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,This is why I call you fools!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:01.16,0:06:02.80,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,King Bradley...
Dialogue: 0,0:06:03.86,0:06:05.84,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,How many times \Ndo I have to kill you...
Dialogue: 0,0:06:11.36,0:06:12.72,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,before you die?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:21.23,0:06:22.27,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Stop!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:23.87,0:06:25.61,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What? What has he done?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:26.42,0:06:27.49,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Gluttony?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:31.57,0:06:33.79,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Alchemic decomposition?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:41.06,0:06:42.34,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,How could you?!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:42.86,0:06:44.84,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I told you, you can't use alchemy!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:45.30,0:06:46.76,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That much more has been lost!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:46.76,0:06:47.59,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Stay back!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:48.67,0:06:50.59,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Do not touch me!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:54.76,0:06:56.93,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What do you think you're doing?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:00.92,0:07:03.14,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother is not dead yet.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:05.22,0:07:07.94,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,See? He's still so warm.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:08.85,0:07:11.24,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,His soul is still inside the gate.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:11.92,0:07:14.45,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,All I have to do is \Nbring it back from there.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:14.91,0:07:17.37,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The way he did so for me.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:17.37,0:07:19.20,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Don't! If you do that...
Dialogue: 0,0:07:19.20,0:07:20.21,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I...
Dialogue: 0,0:07:20.54,0:07:24.69,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,was turned into a Philosopher's Stone because of the sacrifices of many.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:24.69,0:07:30.30,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,No, I might have died \Nback on that day to begin with.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:30.83,0:07:31.93,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Al...
Dialogue: 0,0:07:31.93,0:07:33.05,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Which is why...
Dialogue: 0,0:07:37.33,0:07:38.64,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Watch out.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:45.12,0:07:46.19,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother...
Dialogue: 0,0:09:06.82,0:09:08.84,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Colonel! Colonel!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:08.84,0:09:09.89,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Colonel!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:09.89,0:09:11.23,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Roy Mustang!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:29.36,0:09:30.12,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Al?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:32.26,0:09:33.51,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Wh-What is this?!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:34.56,0:09:36.25,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Where are we?!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:36.25,0:09:37.24,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,At the gate.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:44.51,0:09:46.24,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Where does it go through to?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:46.24,0:09:50.64,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,As I remember, it went to a city called London when I passed through it.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:50.64,0:09:51.93,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's what Pop called it.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:51.93,0:09:55.31,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Pop?! You mean Hohenheim of Light?!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:55.31,0:09:56.37,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:56.37,0:09:58.53,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Then he's still alive!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:05.76,0:10:08.90,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You'd better not. \NThere's no telling what will happen.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:08.90,0:10:10.78,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm going to go see Hohenheim!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:11.30,0:10:14.47,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm going to kill him!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:15.51,0:10:18.68,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Take me to where Hohenheim is!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:32.87,0:10:34.19,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Don't interfere!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:34.74,0:10:36.23,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm going there!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:38.42,0:10:40.22,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The place where Hohenheim is!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:41.09,0:10:42.50,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The place where {\i1}he{\i0} is!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:43.85,0:10:45.53,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The place where Dad is!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:05.83,0:11:06.71,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Al...
Dialogue: 0,0:11:15.32,0:11:17.69,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Ed... you're alive?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:19.64,0:11:20.83,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yeah...
Dialogue: 0,0:11:23.70,0:11:25.64,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Why am I crying?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:27.63,0:11:28.42,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:31.32,0:11:36.17,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Al transmuted you—your dead body.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:39.18,0:11:43.97,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,He used the Philosopher's Stone to restore my body and soul?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:43.97,0:11:45.72,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Then what happened to {\i1}him{\i0}?!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:50.43,0:11:53.31,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Are you telling me that he's gone?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:55.24,0:11:58.16,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Al! Al! Al!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:58.73,0:11:59.81,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Al!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:12.16,0:12:13.37,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,How could this happen?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:14.18,0:12:17.79,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,How could I lose the Philosopher's Stone, \Nin the state I'm in?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:18.58,0:12:21.43,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'll have to get Pride to drive some more foolish humans into a corner.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:30.45,0:12:33.64,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Gluttony? What are you doing here?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:36.16,0:12:37.90,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You must be hungry.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:37.90,0:12:40.90,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Wait! You recognize me, don't you?!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:54.82,0:12:56.04,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Hurry and get going.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:56.55,0:12:59.55,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I hate to ask, \Nbut can you take him too?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:02.80,0:13:04.19,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What about you, Ed?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:04.19,0:13:07.14,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm going to destroy this place
Dialogue: 0,0:13:07.14,0:13:11.09,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,to make sure nobody ever seeks the Philosopher's Stone again.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:11.67,0:13:15.87,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Right. You can come along \Nafterward by yourself, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:15.87,0:13:19.32,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,After all, you've now got some fine legs there.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:25.22,0:13:27.32,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If what Pop said is true,
Dialogue: 0,0:13:28.03,0:13:32.54,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,then right now, Al's body and soul \Nare inside the gate.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:33.12,0:13:35.70,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There can be no other \Nprice for a life.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:35.70,0:13:39.17,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Even if I offer all of myself, it might not do any good.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:40.22,0:13:41.30,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But still,
Dialogue: 0,0:13:41.92,0:13:46.80,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,there's no reason for you to \Nhave to go away. Come back, Al.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:02.87,0:14:04.96,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,How is everyone?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:05.47,0:14:08.74,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Things are finally starting to calm down here in Central.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:09.33,0:14:11.44,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Owing to the Führer's disappearance,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:11.44,0:14:15.64,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\i1}the new government assumed power surprisingly quickly,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:15.64,0:14:20.17,Dialogue,,60,60,0,,{\i1}and the military handed over their political decision-making authority to the Assembly.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:21.28,0:14:23.91,Dialogue,,20,20,20,,{\i1}But it looks like the wars are going to continue
Dialogue: 0,0:14:23.91,0:14:26.01,Dialogue,,20,20,20,,{\i1}against those countries who are attacking us all over.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:30.87,0:14:34.77,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Even so, the policies toward Ishbal \Nhave been reversed,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:34.77,0:14:39.23,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\i1}and I'd like to believe that everything else \Nis getting better, little by little.
Dialogue: 1,0:14:44.60,0:14:48.57,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I think that Brigadier General Mustang's return will still be a while off.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:52.07,0:14:54.45,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Would you stop \Nlooking down like that?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:56.94,0:15:02.42,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The plan was perfect, but I didn't arrive in time, and as a result...
Dialogue: 0,0:15:02.42,0:15:04.81,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There's no such thing as perfect.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:04.81,0:15:06.62,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,This whole world is imperfect.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:08.29,0:15:10.55,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's why it's so beautiful.
Dialogue: 1,0:15:22.99,0:15:26.65,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,How has Alphonse-kun been doing since then?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:28.65,0:15:33.66,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I know that when he was found, he was still a ten-year-old boy,
Dialogue: 1,0:15:33.97,0:15:37.48,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,but I was surprised that he had lost all of his memories
Dialogue: 1,0:15:37.48,0:15:40.03,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,since the day they tried to transmute their mother.
Dialogue: 1,0:15:41.82,0:15:47.17,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Does he still not remember anything that happened?
Dialogue: 1,0:15:47.87,0:15:52.18,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,And will Edward-san really never again...
Dialogue: 0,0:15:56.12,0:15:57.19,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Sensei!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:02.11,0:16:06.05,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,So Ed is really nowhere to be found, after all?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:06.67,0:16:09.19,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Even if someone does \Ngive up their life as the price,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:09.19,0:16:11.28,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,they probably still cannot \Nattain a human transmutation.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:11.65,0:16:14.56,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Maybe the reason why \NAl is in that form
Dialogue: 0,0:16:14.56,0:16:18.02,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,is because the four years of time \Nthey spent together
Dialogue: 0,0:16:18.02,0:16:20.63,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,was the price he had to pay.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:21.37,0:16:25.76,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Al has been reading books on alchemy recently,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:25.76,0:16:27.71,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,the way he did long ago.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:28.20,0:16:31.97,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's almost like he's doing it \Nto keep from forgetting about Ed.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:33.45,0:16:36.68,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,And as for that boy Wrath,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:36.68,0:16:38.97,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Winry put some Automail on him.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:39.65,0:16:42.44,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The ones she had prepared for Ed.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:43.82,0:16:45.17,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Where is he now?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:45.17,0:16:46.94,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,He left.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:48.10,0:16:49.25,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Is that so?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:55.13,0:16:57.24,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You want to study again?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:57.47,0:17:00.24,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Mm-hmm, at your place, Sensei.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:00.55,0:17:01.77,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Is that okay?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:02.96,0:17:05.94,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I want to study more
Dialogue: 0,0:17:05.94,0:17:09.54,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,about alchemy and equivalent exchange.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:09.54,0:17:12.84,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,And one day, \NI want to see Brother again.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:17.68,0:17:20.13,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I don't know what I should do.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:20.13,0:17:23.23,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But if I learn more alchemy, then someday,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:23.49,0:17:24.73,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'll see Brother again.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:25.23,0:17:27.17,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's the feeling I get.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:28.11,0:17:29.19,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Al...
Dialogue: 0,0:17:29.19,0:17:30.32,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Is that all right?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:40.97,0:17:42.79,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I just can't help myself \Nagainst those eyes.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:47.66,0:17:48.98,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Al,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:48.98,0:17:50.54,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,promise me one thing.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:52.12,0:17:54.74,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm going to keep training \Nmore and more
Dialogue: 0,0:17:54.74,0:17:56.63,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,to become the greatest \NAutomail mechanic around.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:57.26,0:18:00.14,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,So promise me that \Nyou'll come home.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:00.67,0:18:03.14,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That you'll come home \Nin one piece.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:04.15,0:18:08.65,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'll be okay. I'll study, and I'm sure I'll find Brother and come home.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:32.98,0:18:35.36,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's enough for today.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:37.73,0:18:41.55,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Thank you for coming along with us, Dr. Hohenheim.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:41.90,0:18:44.75,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Are you all really practicing magic?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:45.38,0:18:48.68,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,In mythology, there is \Nan island named Thule.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:48.68,0:18:53.02,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Those of us in the Thule Society \Nbelieve it to be the land where God dwells,
Dialogue: 0,0:18:53.02,0:18:56.02,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,and we are searching for \Na path that will lead us to it.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:56.02,0:18:59.28,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,With your continued help, \Nwe will work towards that end.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:00.02,0:19:03.12,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I am looking for a path myself,
Dialogue: 0,0:19:03.12,0:19:04.75,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Professor Haushofer.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:18.32,0:19:22.27,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Fourteen marks for just one? \NThat's positively awful.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:22.27,0:19:25.51,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,How long is this inflation \Ngoing to continue?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:50.48,0:19:52.36,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What's going on, Edward?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:52.97,0:19:54.04,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:56.35,0:19:59.86,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Liquid-fuel rockets? Goddard?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:59.86,0:20:01.91,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,He's an American,
Dialogue: 0,0:20:01.91,0:20:05.43,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,but I hear there's another guy in Transylvania doing the same research.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:05.75,0:20:07.59,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,His name's not Dracula, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:07.59,0:20:10.97,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,His name is Oberth, \Nand apparently, he's still a student.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:10.97,0:20:11.77,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm going to go meet him.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:12.34,0:20:14.06,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What will you do \Nonce you meet him?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:14.06,0:20:17.52,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,He's thinking of using rockets to go out into space.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:17.52,0:20:21.70,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Maybe I can get closer to my world \Nby going out into space.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:21.70,0:20:24.13,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There's ether out there, and all.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:24.13,0:20:25.99,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Haven't you read Einstein?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:25.99,0:20:27.41,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That guy is pretty iffy.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:28.79,0:20:32.41,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If you can't use alchemy, you'll use mechanical technology, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:34.39,0:20:39.90,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I should have been able to bind his soul and body together and recreate him.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:39.90,0:20:44.02,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But the next thing I knew, \NI had come to this world by myself.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:44.02,0:20:47.01,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Passing through to here \Nwas the only way
Dialogue: 0,0:20:47.01,0:20:49.16,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,for you to keep from \Nlosing your mind and body.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:49.16,0:20:51.40,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You must have done so unconsciously.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:51.40,0:20:56.38,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But I've once again lost that which \NAl did so much to give me.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:58.10,0:21:01.37,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We can't say that \Neverything is perfect.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:01.37,0:21:04.95,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The whole world is \Nimperfect, after all.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:12.45,0:21:18.05,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I had meant to give my own life as the price for transmuting Al.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:19.18,0:21:21.11,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,And yet, I'm still alive.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:21.77,0:21:26.36,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Maybe I did obtain something \Nwithout paying the price after all.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:26.36,0:21:28.83,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Or maybe Al is still there.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:28.83,0:21:31.52,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You two have been \Njourneying together.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:32.03,0:21:34.22,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The people you met \Nduring that time,
Dialogue: 0,0:21:34.22,0:21:37.27,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,the things you saw, \Nyour pain, your effort,
Dialogue: 0,0:21:37.98,0:21:39.97,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,everything that you experienced...
Dialogue: 0,0:21:41.02,0:21:44.24,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That could be the price you paid, couldn't it?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:56.69,0:22:01.25,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I don't know right now what \NI should do to get back to you.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:02.31,0:22:05.34,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But you can bet that \NI'm coming back.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:05.70,0:22:07.75,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\i1}We'll meet again, Al!
Dialogue: 0,0:22:12.78,0:22:17.29,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Man must pay an equal price in order to obtain anything.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:17.85,0:22:19.87,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That is the Law of Equivalent Exchange.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:20.82,0:22:25.50,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,At the time, we believed that \Nto be the true way of the world.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:26.40,0:22:29.82,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\i1}But the real world is imperfect,
Dialogue: 0,0:22:29.82,0:22:34.37,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\i1}and there was no law that could explain everything.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:35.20,0:22:37.87,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Same with the Law of Equivalent Exchange.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:38.63,0:22:40.58,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Even so, we believe...
Dialogue: 0,0:22:41.28,0:22:44.59,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,that man cannot obtain anything \Nwithout paying a price.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:45.47,0:22:47.57,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The pain that we received
Dialogue: 0,0:22:47.57,0:22:51.05,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,must have been the price \Nwe paid to obtain something.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:51.60,0:22:53.93,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,And by paying the price of effort,
Dialogue: 0,0:22:53.93,0:22:58.85,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,everyone will certainly be able to obtain something.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:59.38,0:23:02.98,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Equivalent exchange is not the law of the world.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:02.98,0:23:05.07,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\i1}That's the promise Brother \Nand I made with each other
Dialogue: 0,0:23:06.09,0:23:08.81,Dialogue,,0,0,20,,{\i1}until the day we meet again.
